
# 📌 Product Price History Tracker

**Multi-Platform Price Monitoring System**

A backend-focused system to track **daily product prices across multiple e-commerce platforms** (Amazon, Flipkart, etc.) and expose them via REST APIs for frontend consumption.

> Think **PriceBefore / Keepa**, but simpler, cleaner, and academically solid.

---

## 🎯 Project Objective

Track and store **historical prices** of products sold on different platforms so users can:

- See today’s price
- Compare prices across platforms
- Analyze price trends over time
- Make better buying decisions

---

## 🧠 Problem Statement

- Same product → different prices on different platforms
- Prices fluctuate daily
- Existing platforms show only current price, not structured historical data

This project solves that by maintaining a **normalized price history database** and exposing it via APIs.

---

## 👥 Target Users

- End users looking for the best time to buy a product
- Developers consuming price-history APIs

*(Alerts, watchlists, and automation are future scope)*

---

## 🏗️ System Architecture

```
Client (React)
   ↓ REST API
Spring Boot Backend
   ↓ JPA/Hibernate
MySQL Database
```

- Frontend never interacts with DB directly
- Backend handles all business logic

---

## 🗄️ Database Schema

### 1️⃣ Users

```
users
-----
id (PK)
name
email
password
```

---

### 2️⃣ Products

```
products
--------
id (PK)
name
brand
category
image_url
```

---

### 3️⃣ Platforms

```
platforms
---------
id (PK)
name
logo_url
```

---

### 4️⃣ Product Price History (Core Table)

```
product_price_history
---------------------
id (PK)
product_id (FK → products)
platform_id (FK → platforms)
price
date
```

✔ One row = price of one product on one platform on one date

